From 3a44f20c7bc66db1da583e8a6f0ab740e31908e9 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: goldislead <69987043+goldislead@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 28 Aug 2026 20:19:01 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] [GPU] Replace AC6 ground hack with scalar approximation
 rounding

The exact precision and halfway behavior still isn't confirmed, but this builds on Edge's work and fixes 4E4D07D1 without ever touching vertex indices.

EXP, LOG, LOGC, RCP, RCPC, RCPF, RSQ, RSQC, RSQF, and SQRT results are all rounded to 21 mantissa bits in the translators and interpreter.

DXBC builds reciprocal with DIV and reciprocal square root with SQRT followed by DIV so its own approx RCP and RSQ aren't rounded again. SPIR-V keeps InverseSqrt since Vulkan gives it a tighter error bound.

SPIR-V only passes scalars through ZeroIfAnyOperandIsZero, so the unreachable vector handling is dropped and the exponent bits are checked without shifting them first.

Co-Authored-By: Herman S. <429230+has207@users.noreply.github.com>
